  "figure": {
    "caption": "Alignment by the Markov chain of [Kedia2022Alignment], connected setting: each particle carries one of $q$ orientations (here $q = 3$, shown as three colours). One particle at a time (outlined) either steps, expanding into a free neighbouring node and contracting forward with a probability that grows with its gain in neighbours ($\\lambda$) and in agreeing neighbours ($\\gamma$), or turns to a new orientation, accepted with a probability that grows with its gain in agreeing neighbours; moves that would disconnect the system or create a hole are refused. Shown is a run in which every proposed move is accepted. For large biases most particles end up sharing one orientation, with high probability; for small biases they do not.",
